# Project documentation

Read `AGENTS.md` at the start of every session.

## Canonical files

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `AGENTS.md` | Agent onboarding, status, process pointer |
| `docs/PROCESS.md` | Scope → ADR → HLD → LLD → ship |
| `docs/scope.md` | Product job, must / later / never |
| `docs/adr/` | One ADR per feature |
| `docs/hld/` | HLD for the feature in flight |
| `docs/lld/` | LLD for the feature in flight |
| `docs/README.md` | Index |
| `docs/CHANGELOG.md` | Structural doc changes |
| `README.md` | Human overview |

Retired (not requirements): files listed in `docs/archive/README.md`, including the old V1 spec, DESIGN, LEARNINGS, and Figma/mockup plans.

## When to update

- **Product job / must-have change** → `docs/scope.md`
- **How we build a feature** → that feature’s ADR, then HLD, then LLD. No whole-product ADR
- **New doc file** → `docs/README.md`, `AGENTS.md` map, `docs/CHANGELOG.md`
- **Onboarding / status** → `AGENTS.md` and `README.md`
- **Any markdown prose edit** → `@humanize-docs`

## Dual sync

Local repo wins. After material doc changes, sync a summary to the Notion Project Hub (`@maintain-project-docs`). Commit only when the user asks.

## Implementation gate

No `src/` changes until the in-flight feature has an **Accepted** ADR, agreed HLD, and agreed LLD. Do not implement from `docs/archive/` or from the retired V1 spec.
